@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
+# Oracle Desktop Runtime
+
+## Scope
+
+Windows/Linux local Oracle MySQL backend and packaging. The default product
+engine preference currently remains SQLite/cloud; selection of this local
+backend is a subsequent integration requirement. macOS bundle/signing, Android
+server integration and native iOS hosting remain implementation gaps. Never
+report those platforms as delivered based on portable source or desktop tests.
+
+## Interfaces And Transport
+
+- `NativeMySqlDatabase({MethodChannel? channel, LocalMySqlRuntime? runtime})`:
+  an explicit channel wins. Otherwise desktop calls use the injected/shared
+  runtime; Android/OHOS/iOS retain their existing channel path for now.
+- `LocalMySqlRuntime.invoke(method, arguments)` accepts `query` and
+  `executeScript`. `schema` is a schema name, including empty server scope;
+  `source` is SQL, `params` is nullable strings for prepared queries.
+- `MySqlFfi.invoke(libraryPath, request)` runs the real C client on an isolate.
+  `qfli_mysql_invoke(const char*, size_t)` returns allocated UTF-8 JSON, freed
+  only with `qfli_mysql_free`. Request fields add `method`, `socket`, `password`.
+- `query`, `executeScript`, `shutdown` share the existing typed result shape.
+  Script summary fields occupy the outer object; `results` are ordered results.
+  No double conversion of BIGINT/DECIMAL; binary fields are hex; NULL stays null.
+- Default display limits are 1,000 rows/1 MiB; optional `rowLimit` and `byteLimit`
+  can only lower them. Scripts drain every Oracle result, retaining at most 128.
+- New credentialed C++ overloads retain all existing OHOS signatures and symbols.
+  Windows fixes `MYSQL_PROTOCOL_PIPE` and enables
+  `MYSQL_OPT_GET_SERVER_PUBLIC_KEY` for Oracle caching_sha2_password RSA exchange.
+  Linux/macOS use `MYSQL_PROTOCOL_SOCKET`. Neither can fall back to TCP.
+
+## Lifecycle And Files
+
+Default data is `<local-application-data>/qfli_sql/mysql`; Windows uses
+LOCALAPPDATA, Linux XDG_DATA_HOME or ~/.local/share, macOS Application Support.
+`QFLI_MYSQL_BUNDLE` overrides installed bundle discovery. The explicit constructor
+supports isolated fixtures. Production must not set the test `serverUser=root`.
+
+`runtime.lock` is held for the server lifetime; a canonical directory registry
+rejects duplicate owners in the same isolate. Initialization creates a private
+staging directory, invokes upstream `--initialize-insecure`, and moves only a
+successful datadir to `data`. `initialized.json` stores the exact Oracle version
+and random 256-bit credential. `root.sql` sets it before readiness checks.
+Missing metadata beside existing data, malformed metadata or a changed version
+returns unavailable; `--upgrade=NONE` prevents implicit upgrades. Recovery of
+such metadata is a separate explicit operation, never deletion of user data.
+
+Unix directories are 700, credential files 600 and sockets use a short private
+temporary parent. Windows storage inherits the user's local application ACL;
+pipe names are unpredictable and queries require the stored credential. Server
+startup disables TCP, mysqlx, LOCAL INFILE and filesystem import/export. It uses
+bundled plugin/message paths and modest embedded-service memory settings.
+
+`invoke` and `stop()` serialize. Graceful stop uses Oracle shutdown, bounded
+wait, then owned-process termination. Cleanup releases directory ownership even
+if socket cleanup fails. Linux launcher validates the app parent then sets
+PDEATHSIG; Windows uses a creation-time Job Object and waits on the app handle.
+Normal exit and application death leave data for upstream InnoDB recovery.
+
+## Packaging
+
+`native/mysql/desktop/CMakeLists.txt` builds the client bridge and launcher.
+Windows/Linux FFI plugin builds include it and install `qfli_mysql/{bin,lib,share}`
+beside the app. Missing server/source inputs fail desktop packaging. Windows
+Oracle/OpenSSL DLLs are resolved from bridge directory through LoadLibraryExW;
+Linux client uses $ORIGIN RPATH and the child uses its bundled lib directory.
+
+Use the hash-verified 8.4.6 official Windows ZIP and its retained licenses/docs.
+Linux staging copies installed Oracle packages, complete dependency resolution,
+resources/plugins and license inputs. Keep provenance and host libc prerequisites
+explicit. CMake requires verified Oracle source RapidJSON headers; no ad hoc JSON
+serializer or replacement SQL engine is allowed.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Standalone lifecycle test: actual upstream initialization/version/private
+  transport, ownership, exact prepared values, metadata/NULL/binary, diagnostics,
+  transactions/partial scripts, caps/result draining, credentials/no fallback,
+  persistence/stop/restart, version rejection, app death and crash recovery.
+- Typed adapter tests: set `QFLI_MYSQL_TEST_BUNDLE` to a built bundle; assert exact
+  data, script results/errors and missing-runtime behavior. No mock establishes
+  real native functionality. Existing explicit-channel tests must keep passing.
+- Available evidence: Windows 8.4.6, Linux 8.0.46, complete installed runtime
+  bundles, Windows Flutter tests. MSVC/full desktop GUIs and Apple execution
+  are not established by these checks.
+
+## Wrong Vs Correct
+
+Wrong: enable TCP when a socket/pipe login fails, split scripts by semicolons,
+replace a version-mismatched datadir, or change the old OHOS C++ ABI.
+
+Correct: return the real error, use Oracle's prepared/multi-statement client,
+keep persistent data and retain old symbols alongside credentialed overloads.
diff --git a/lib/local_mysql_runtime.dart b/lib/local_mysql_runtime.dart
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ac96803
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/local_mysql_runtime.dart
@@ -0,0 +1,451 @@
+import 'dart:async';
+import 'dart:convert';
+import 'dart:io';
+import 'dart:math';
+
+import 'package:path/path.dart' as p;
+
+import 'mysql_ffi.dart';
+
+/// Owns one app-private Oracle server; the launcher handles application death.
+class LocalMySqlRuntime {
+  LocalMySqlRuntime({
+    required this.bundleDirectory,
+    required this.dataDirectory,
+    required this.libraryPath,
+    required this.launcherPath,
+    this.serverPath,
+    this.serverUser,
+    this.readinessTimeout = const Duration(seconds: 45),
+  });
+
+  static bool get supported =>
+      Platform.isWindows || Platform.isLinux || Platform.isMacOS;
+
+  static final LocalMySqlRuntime shared = _discover();
+  static final Set<String> _ownedDirectories = {};
+
+  final Directory bundleDirectory;
+  final Directory dataDirectory;
+  final String libraryPath;
+  final String launcherPath;
+  final String? serverPath;
+  // Only explicit host fixtures may ask mysqld to run as root.
+  final String? serverUser;
+  final Duration readinessTimeout;
+  Future<void> _tail = Future<void>.value();
+  Process? _server;
+  Future<int>? _serverExit;
+  int? _exitCode;
+  Directory? _ipcDirectory;
+  RandomAccessFile? _lock;
+  String? _ownedDirectory;
+  String? _socket;
+  String? _password;
+  String _diagnostics = '';
+
+  Future<Map<String, Object?>> invoke(
+    String method,
+    Map<String, Object?> arguments,
+  ) => _serialize(() async {
+    if (method != 'query' && method != 'executeScript') {
+      throw ArgumentError.value(method, 'method');
+    }
+    try {
+      await _ensureReady();
+      return await _call(method, arguments);
+    } on Object catch (error) {
+      return _failure(error.toString(), script: method == 'executeScript');
+    }
+  });
+
+  Future<void> stop() => _serialize(_stop);
+
+  Future<T> _serialize<T>(Future<T> Function() action) {
+    final result = _tail.then((_) => action());
+    _tail = result.then<void>((_) {}, onError: (Object _, StackTrace _) {});
+    return result;
+  }
+
+  Future<Map<String, Object?>> _call(
+    String method,
+    Map<String, Object?> arguments,
+  ) => MySqlFfi.invoke(libraryPath, {
+    ...arguments,
+    'method': method,
+    'socket': _socket,
+    'password': _password,
+  });
+
+  Future<void> _ensureReady() async {
+    if (_server != null && _exitCode == null) return;
+    await _stop();
+    if (!supported) {
+      throw UnsupportedError('Local Oracle MySQL requires a desktop host.');
+    }
+    final server =
+        serverPath ??
+        p.join(
+          bundleDirectory.path,
+          'bin',
+          Platform.isWindows ? 'mysqld.exe' : 'mysqld',
+        );
+    for (final path in [server, launcherPath, libraryPath]) {
+      if (!await File(path).exists()) {
+        throw StateError('Missing bundled MySQL file: $path');
+      }
+    }
+    await dataDirectory.create(recursive: true);
+    await _makePrivate(dataDirectory.path);
+    final resolved = await dataDirectory.resolveSymbolicLinks();
+    final owned = Platform.isWindows ? resolved.toLowerCase() : resolved;
+    if (!_ownedDirectories.add(owned)) {
+      throw StateError('The local MySQL data directory is already in use.');
+    }
+    _ownedDirectory = owned;
+    RandomAccessFile? lock;
+    try {
+      lock = await File(
+        p.join(dataDirectory.path, 'runtime.lock'),
+      ).open(mode: FileMode.append);
+      await lock.lock(FileLock.exclusive);
+      _lock = lock;
+    } on Object {
+      await lock?.close();
+      _ownedDirectories.remove(owned);
+      _ownedDirectory = null;
+      throw StateError('The local MySQL data directory is already in use.');
+    }
+    try {
+      final versionResult = await _run(server, ['--no-defaults', '--version']);
+      final version = RegExp(
+        r'\bVer\s+(8\.\d+\.\d+[^\s]*)',
+      ).firstMatch(versionResult)?.group(1);
+      if (version == null || versionResult.contains('MariaDB')) {
+        throw StateError(
+          'The bundled server must be Oracle MySQL 8.x: $versionResult',
+        );
+      }
+      final data = Directory(p.join(dataDirectory.path, 'data'));
+      final marker = File(p.join(dataDirectory.path, 'initialized.json'));
+      if (await marker.exists()) {
+        final raw = jsonDecode(await marker.readAsString());
+        if (raw is! Map ||
+            raw['version'] != version ||
+            raw['password'] is! String ||
+            !RegExp(r'^[a-f0-9]{64}$').hasMatch(raw['password'] as String) ||
+            !await data.exists()) {
+          throw StateError(
+            'MySQL initialization metadata or server version does not match. Automatic upgrade is disabled.',
+          );
+        }
+        _password = raw['password'] as String;
+      } else {
+        if (await data.exists()) {
+          throw StateError(
+            'MySQL data exists without successful initialization metadata.',
+          );
+        }
+        final staging = await dataDirectory.createTemp('initializing-');
+        await _makePrivate(staging.path);
+        try {
+          await _run(server, [
+            '--no-defaults',
+            '--initialize-insecure',
+            '--basedir=${bundleDirectory.path}',
+            '--datadir=${staging.path}',
+            '--performance-schema=OFF',
+            '--innodb-buffer-pool-size=32M',
+            '--innodb-redo-log-capacity=16M',
+            if (serverUser != null) '--user=$serverUser',
+          ], timeout: const Duration(minutes: 3));
+          _password = _randomHex(32);
+          final pending = File(
+            p.join(dataDirectory.path, 'initialized.pending.json'),
+          );
+          await pending.writeAsString(
+            jsonEncode({'version': version, 'password': _password}),
+            flush: true,
+          );
+          await _makePrivate(pending.path, directory: false);
+          await staging.rename(data.path);
+          await pending.rename(marker.path);
+        } finally {
+          if (await staging.exists()) await staging.delete(recursive: true);
+        }
+      }
+      // A per-datadir lock stays held for the server's lifetime. Unix sockets
+      // use a short private temporary directory to fit sockaddr_un on macOS.
+      if (Platform.isWindows) {
+        _socket = 'qfli_mysql_${_randomHex(16)}';
+      } else {
+        _ipcDirectory = await Directory.systemTemp.createTemp('qfli-mysql-');
+        await _makePrivate(_ipcDirectory!.path);
+        _socket = p.join(_ipcDirectory!.path, 'mysql.sock');
+      }
+      final init = File(p.join(dataDirectory.path, 'root.sql'));
+      await init.writeAsString(
+        "ALTER USER 'root'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY '$_password';\n",
+        flush: true,
+      );
+      await _makePrivate(init.path, directory: false);
+      final process = await _start(server, [
+        '--no-defaults',
+        '--basedir=${bundleDirectory.path}',
+        '--datadir=${data.path}',
+        '--plugin-dir=${p.join(bundleDirectory.path, 'lib', 'plugin')}',
+        '--lc-messages-dir=${p.join(bundleDirectory.path, 'share')}',
+        '--socket=$_socket',
+        '--skip-networking',
+        '--mysqlx=0',
+        '--skip-log-bin',
+        '--performance-schema=OFF',
+        '--max-connections=20',
+        '--table-open-cache=64',
+        if (Platform.isWindows) '--named-pipe',
+        if (serverUser != null) '--user=$serverUser',
+        '--upgrade=NONE',
+        '--local-infile=0',
+        '--secure-file-priv=NULL',
+        '--max-allowed-packet=8M',
+        '--innodb-buffer-pool-size=32M',
+        '--innodb-redo-log-capacity=16M',
+        '--init-file=${init.path}',
+        '--pid-file=${p.join(dataDirectory.path, 'mysqld.pid')}',
+        '--log-error=${p.join(dataDirectory.path, 'mysqld.log')}',
+      ]);
+      _server = process;
+      _exitCode = null;
+      _serverExit = process.exitCode.then((code) {
+        _exitCode = code;
+        return code;
+      });
+      _drain(process);
+      final deadline = DateTime.now().add(readinessTimeout);
+      Object? readinessError;
+      while (_exitCode == null && DateTime.now().isBefore(deadline)) {
+        final ready = await _call('query', {
+          'schema': '',
+          'source': 'SELECT VERSION(), @@version_comment',
+          'params': <String?>[],
+        });
+        readinessError = ready['error'];
+        if (ready['available'] == true && ready['exitCode'] == 0) {
+          final rows = ready['rows'] as List;
+          if ((rows.first as List).first != version ||
+              rows.toString().contains('MariaDB')) {
+            throw StateError(
+              'The private MySQL server version does not match its bundle.',
+            );
+          }
+          return;
+        }
+        await Future<void>.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 100));
+      }
+      final log = File(p.join(dataDirectory.path, 'mysqld.log'));
+      final details = await log.exists()
+          ? await log.readAsString()
+          : _diagnostics;
+      throw StateError(
+        'Oracle MySQL did not become ready (exit $_exitCode, $readinessError): ${details.length > 8192 ? details.substring(details.length - 8192) : details}',
+      );
+    } on Object {
+      await _stop();
+      rethrow;
+    }
+  }
+
+  Future<Process> _start(
+    String server,
+    List<String> arguments,
+  ) => Process.start(
+    launcherPath,
+    ['$pid', server, ...arguments],
+    workingDirectory: bundleDirectory.path,
+    environment: {
+      if (Platform.isWindows)
+        'PATH':
+            '${p.join(bundleDirectory.path, 'bin')};${p.join(bundleDirectory.path, 'lib')};${Platform.environment['PATH'] ?? ''}',
+      if (Platform.isLinux)
+        'LD_LIBRARY_PATH':
+            '${p.join(bundleDirectory.path, 'lib')}:${Platform.environment['LD_LIBRARY_PATH'] ?? ''}',
+    },
+  );
+
+  Future<String> _run(
+    String server,
+    List<String> arguments, {
+    Duration timeout = const Duration(seconds: 15),
+  }) async {
+    final process = await _start(server, arguments);
+    final output = StringBuffer();
+    void collect(String value) {
+      if (output.length < 8192) output.write(value);
+    }
+
+    final stdoutDone = process.stdout
+        .transform(const Utf8Decoder(allowMalformed: true))
+        .forEach(collect);
+    final stderrDone = process.stderr
+        .transform(const Utf8Decoder(allowMalformed: true))
+        .forEach(collect);
+    int status;
+    try {
+      status = await process.exitCode.timeout(timeout);
+    } on Object {
+      process.kill(ProcessSignal.sigkill);
+      await process.exitCode;
+      rethrow;
+    } finally {
+      await Future.wait([stdoutDone, stderrDone]);
+    }
+    if (status != 0) {
+      throw StateError('MySQL command failed ($status): $output');
+    }
+    return output.toString();
+  }
+
+  void _drain(Process process) {
+    _diagnostics = '';
+    void collect(String value) {
+      _diagnostics += value;
+      if (_diagnostics.length > 8192) {
+        _diagnostics = _diagnostics.substring(_diagnostics.length - 8192);
+      }
+    }
+
+    process.stdout
+        .transform(const Utf8Decoder(allowMalformed: true))
+        .listen(collect);
+    process.stderr
+        .transform(const Utf8Decoder(allowMalformed: true))
+        .listen(collect);
+  }
+
+  Future<void> _stop() async {
+    final process = _server;
+    try {
+      if (process != null) {
+        if (_exitCode == null) {
+          try {
+            await _call('shutdown', {});
+          } on Object {
+            process.kill();
+          }
+        }
+        try {
+          await _serverExit!.timeout(const Duration(seconds: 10));
+        } on TimeoutException {
+          process.kill(ProcessSignal.sigkill);
+          await _serverExit;
+        }
+      }
+    } finally {
+      _server = null;
+      _serverExit = null;
+      _exitCode = null;
+      _socket = null;
+      _password = null;
+      final ipc = _ipcDirectory;
+      _ipcDirectory = null;
+      final lock = _lock;
+      _lock = null;
+      final owned = _ownedDirectory;
+      _ownedDirectory = null;
+      try {
+        if (ipc != null && await ipc.exists()) {
+          await ipc.delete(recursive: true);
+        }
+      } finally {
+        try {
+          if (lock != null) {
+            try {
+              await lock.unlock();
+            } finally {
+              await lock.close();
+            }
+          }
+        } finally {
+          if (owned != null) _ownedDirectories.remove(owned);
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
+  static Future<void> _makePrivate(String path, {bool directory = true}) async {
+    if (Platform.isWindows) return;
+    final result = await Process.run('/bin/chmod', [
+      directory ? '700' : '600',
+      path,
+    ]);
+    if (result.exitCode != 0) {
+      throw FileSystemException('Cannot make MySQL storage private.', path);
+    }
+  }
+
+  static String _randomHex(int bytes) {
+    final random = Random.secure();
+    return List.generate(
+      bytes,
+      (_) => random.nextInt(256).toRadixString(16).padLeft(2, '0'),
+    ).join();
+  }
+
+  static Map<String, Object?> _failure(String error, {required bool script}) =>
+      {
+        'available': false,
+        'exitCode': 127,
+        'error': error,
+        'sqlState': '',
+        'columns': <String>[],
+        'columnInfo': <Object>[],
+        'rows': <Object>[],
+        'affectedRows': 0,
+        'truncated': false,
+        if (script) 'results': <Object>[],
+      };
+
+  static LocalMySqlRuntime _discover() {
+    final app = p.dirname(Platform.resolvedExecutable);
+    final configured = Platform.environment['QFLI_MYSQL_BUNDLE'];
+    final bundle = Directory(
+      configured ??
+          (Platform.isMacOS
+              ? p.normalize(p.join(app, '..', 'Resources', 'qfli_mysql'))
+              : p.join(app, 'qfli_mysql')),
+    );
+    final home =
+        Platform.environment[Platform.isWindows ? 'USERPROFILE' : 'HOME'];
+    if (home == null) {
+      throw StateError('Cannot locate application-private MySQL storage.');
+    }
+    final String root;
+    if (Platform.isWindows) {
+      root =
+          Platform.environment['LOCALAPPDATA'] ??
+          p.join(home, 'AppData', 'Local');
+    } else if (Platform.isMacOS) {
+      root = p.join(home, 'Library', 'Application Support');
+    } else {
+      root =
+          Platform.environment['XDG_DATA_HOME'] ??
+          p.join(home, '.local', 'share');
+    }
+    return LocalMySqlRuntime(
+      bundleDirectory: bundle,
+      dataDirectory: Directory(p.join(root, 'qfli_sql', 'mysql')),
+      launcherPath: p.join(
+        bundle.path,
+        'bin',
+        Platform.isWindows ? 'qfli_mysql_launcher.exe' : 'qfli_mysql_launcher',
+      ),
+      libraryPath: p.join(
+        bundle.path,
+        Platform.isWindows ? 'bin' : 'lib',
+        Platform.isWindows
+            ? 'qfli_mysql_bridge.dll'
+            : 'libqfli_mysql_bridge.${Platform.isMacOS ? 'dylib' : 'so'}',
+      ),
+    );
+  }
+}
